      {
        "insert": "\n\n3 Check RAM\nMethod 1: Using Task Manager (Quickest)"
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "header": 3
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "insert": "This is the easiest way to see your RAM speed and type without installing anything.\nPress "
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "Ctrl + Shift + Esc"
      },
      {
        "insert": " to open the "
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "Task Manager"
      },
      {
        "insert": "."
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "list": "ordered"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "insert": "Click on the "
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "Performance"
      },
      {
        "insert": " tab (if you don't see tabs, click \"More details\" at the bottom)."
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "list": "ordered"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "insert": "Click on "
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "Memory"
      },
      {
        "insert": " in the left sidebar."
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "list": "ordered"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "insert": "Look for "
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "Speed"
      },
      {
        "insert": " (e.g., 2400 MHz, 3200 MHz). While it doesn't always explicitly say \"DDR4,\" you can cross-reference the speed:"
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "list": "ordered"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "DDR3:"
      },
      {
        "insert": " Usually runs between 800 MHz and 2133 MHz."
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "indent": 1,
          "list": "bullet"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "bold": true
        },
        "insert": "DDR4:"
      },
      {
        "insert": " Usually runs between 2133 MHz and 3200+ MHz"
      },
      {
        "attributes": {
          "indent": 1,
          "list": "bullet"
        },
        "insert": "\n"
